d runner. I'll annotate its result when it completes, and that is the cycle's last act.\n\nWhere cycle 143 stands:\n- **Session 2 is done:** `D1_ring_p4s02_20261003_110001.vi` (84cac487) is the adopted file for P4 session 2. It has 53 Error List items. The 2 above the 51 predicted turned out to be by design: the loop-1.2 stop terminal and the read of the stop flag sit open between sessions, and session 3's first action wires them. The miss was in our prediction rule, which is now fixed.\n- **Three defects in our tools and plan, all fixed:** the Error List prediction rule, the re-bind check that refused node ids LabVIEW handed out again after our own deletes, and a wrong terminal name in session 3's plan.\n- **Session 3 is ready to launch:** plan da66a030, predicted peak 676.4 MB against the 680 limit, 56 Error List items predicted, both recipes pass the dry run and the pre-run checks 16/0.\n- **Next cycle's first act:** one scratch run of session 3 on a byte copy of the session-2 file, adopted if every check passes, with session-4 prep beside it. This is in `next.json` and STATUS `## NEXT`.\n\nNone of the sub-agents could commit (`git add` needs approval), so the runner's end-of-cycle commit will carry the files.","ttft_ms":1903,"type":"result","duration_ms":3184182,"uuid":"0539aab0-54f1-485c-bdb1-fa5c3712c72d","ttft_stream_ms":1676,"time_to_request_ms":183,"first_content_frame_ms":1676,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":6}
